  "question": {
    "text": "For any complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi></math>, let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>]</mo></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> be real numbers such that for all complex numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math> satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math> lies on the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Then which of the following statements is(are) TRUE?"
  },
